WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.240
The teaser trailer for Mary Poppins Returns
just dropped with a sugary dose of nostalgia

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.160
and a first look at the magical nanny played
by Emily Blunt.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.500
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and this is my teaser trailer breakdown for

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.430
the Mary Poppins sequel where I'll be explaining
some cool easter eggs and other details you

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.430
might have missed.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.769
And be sure to let me know in the comments
about anything you spotted too!

00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:25.130
It looks like Oscar-winning costume designer
Sandy Powell has done a wonderful job with

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.210
the characters' costumes.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:31.039
In fact, the new film includes an easter egg
to the original movie in the form of the robin

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:32.860
on Mary Poppins' hat.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.200
That little decorative bird is a call-back
to the robin which featured in the song A

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.450
Spoonful of Sugar and which accompanied Mary
as she sang to the Banks children about how

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.980
to tidy up their room.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:50.900
And the new teaser trailer also includes another
tribute to that famous song in the scene where

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.430
Emily Blunt's Mary admires her reflection
in the mirror before walking away, only for

00:00:55.430 --> 00:01:00.030
her reflection to stay behind, watching and
raising an eyebrow as Mary leaves.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.280
That's a throwback to the mirror which Julie
Andrews' Mary took out of her carpet bag and

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.909
put on the wall in the Banks family's home.

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:10.950
And when she was readying to leave the house,
putting on her hat and coat in front of that

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.170
mirror, her reflection took on a life of its
own and joined her in singing A Spoonful of

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.899
Sugar, before watching Mary leave and then
winking!

00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:23.409
And if you look carefully, you can see this
movie's version of Mary's parrot-head umbrella,

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:27.270
which, apparently is going to be able to talk,
just like it did in the first film.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.009
"And if you think I'm keeping my mouth shut..."

00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:34.210
"That will be quite enough, thank you."

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:38.920
Of course, the sequel is returning to Cherry
Tree Lane and, once again, we'll be meeting

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.380
the Banks's neighbour Admiral Boom, whose
ship-inspired home has been updated for the

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.539
new movie.

00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:49.259
The filmmakers have explained that although
the sequel is not going to be an exact reproduction,

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:51.970
it will have familiar elements from the first
film.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.840
In fact, according to the movie's production
designer, "[they] want [us] to feel like [we're]

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.450
seeing something [we've] seen before, but
[we're] really seeing it for the first time."

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.499
As well as Admiral Boom, Mr Binnacle is also
returning for the sequel, though they'll both

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:05.780
be played by new actors.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:12.150
And I wonder if their habit of firing a ship's
cannon twice daily will also be making a come-back?

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.950
Also here in the shot of Cherry Tree Lane
is what looks like a Milkman pushing a crate

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.280
of milk bottles.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.659
The Milkman is a new character for the sequel
and appeared in author P.L.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:24.330
Travers book, Mary Poppins Opens The Door.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:29.360
And just as Admiral Boom's house in Cherry
Tree Lane draws on the one in the 1964 classic

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.330
without being exactly the same, so too the
kite we see in the trailer is clearly inspired

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:38.299
by the green kite with a yellow trim which
belonged to the Banks children in the original

00:02:38.299 --> 00:02:39.489
film.

00:02:39.489 --> 00:02:43.819
And like that original kite, the one in the
new film has clippings from the Times newspaper

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:49.390
on it and its tail is also made from one of
the 'Votes for Women' sashes worn by Mrs Banks.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:54.590
This shot here also looks like a literal hat
tip to the original Mr Banks as he has a similar

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:59.250
look and, if you remember, in the classic
film Mr Banks had his bowler hat punched through

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:03.740
when he was sacked from the bank just before
he returned home for the "Let's Go Fly A Kite"

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.819
song with his children/family.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:10.540
Now, if you're a little unclear on the movie's
timeline, the sequel takes place 20 or so

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.000
years after the original which was set in
1910.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:19.159
That means Mary Poppins Returns will take
place in 1930s depression-era London.

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:23.810
Michael and Jane are now grown up and Michael
has three children: Georgie, Annabel and John,

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.940
who are the three new children we see in the
trailer.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.329
Michael and Jane are obviously delighted to
see Mary Poppins again and, according to the

00:03:31.329 --> 00:03:35.549
movie's synopsis, the magical nanny returns
to the Banks family after Michael suffers

00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:36.960
a personal loss.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.430
Together with the street lamplighter Jack,
who's played by Lin-Manuel Miranda of Hamilton

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:46.670
and Moana fame, Mary Poppins will use "her
unique magical skills to help the family rediscover

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.469
the joy and wonder missing in their lives."

00:03:49.469 --> 00:03:53.129
On the subject of fun, if you were concerned
about the rather dark colour palette in the

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:57.689
trailer, then I think this might just be how
the movie sets up the story.

00:03:57.689 --> 00:04:01.500
First of all, it's set during the Great Depression,
Michael has lost his wife, and the weather

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.280
is literally dark and stormy.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.770
But as we saw in the first film, changes in
the wind signal Mary Poppins coming and going.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.830
And the moment she appears in the teaser,
the sky starts to brighten and we get stronger

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:13.920
colours.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.150
Disney has also released some promo photos
from other scenes that aren't in the trailer

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.900
and they give us a good hint of some of the
fun, colourful moments we can look forward

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.620
to in the final film.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.860
So, what did you think of the teaser trailer
for Mary Poppins Returns?

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:29.919
And were there any other cool details you
spotted?

00:04:29.919 --> 00:04:32.430
Let me know what you thought in the comments
below.

